For recent in-state customer transactions (orders shipped within the home state), sales tax is applied consistently at the **standard state rate of 7%**. This is confirmed by:  

- Explicit policy stating sales tax uses the standard state rate for in-state shipments;  
- Recent tax filings (Q1 and Q2 of this year) applying this rate uniformly;  
- 18 months of audit logs showing no deviations from this practice;  
- Example transactions (e.g., $200 subtotal → $14 tax, $350 → $24.50, etc.) all calculating to a 7% tax rate.

For recent in-state customer orders (shipped within the company’s home state), sales tax is applied at a **consistent standard state rate of 7%** of the order subtotal. This is confirmed by:  

- Explicit policy stating sales tax uses the "standard state rate" for in-state shipments;  
- Recent tax filings (Q1 and Q2 of the year) applying this rate consistently;  
- Audit logs from the past 18 months showing no deviations;  
- Example transactions (e.g., $200 subtotal → $14 tax, $350 → $24.50, etc.) all calculating to 7% of the subtotal.

For recent in-state transactions (orders shipped within the company’s home state), sales tax is applied consistently at a standard state rate of 7%. This is confirmed by:  

- Explicit policy stating the standard state rate applies to in-state shipments;  
- Recent tax filings (Q1 and Q2 of this year) using this rate without variation;  
- Audit logs from the past 18 months showing no deviation from the rate;  
- Example transactions (e.g., $200 subtotal → $14 tax, $350 → $24.50, etc.) all calculating to a 7% tax rate.

For recent in-state transactions (orders shipped within the company’s home state), sales tax is applied **consistently at a standard state rate of 7%**. This is confirmed by:  

- Explicit policy stating the standard state rate applies to in-state shipments;  
- Recent tax filings (Q1 and Q2 of this year) using this rate without deviation;  
- Audit logs from the past 18 months showing no changes to the application of this rate;  
- Example transactions (e.g., Order #A4421: $200 subtotal → $14 tax = 7%; Order #A4502: $350 → $24.50 = 7%, etc.) all reflecting the 7% rate.
